Section 7 - Definitions
(9)
For the purpose of this Policy:
Electronic Message:
a message can be text, graphics or a combination of those;
using an internet or other carriage service such as the internet or a mobile telephone service;
to an electronic address (eg: Email addresses or telephone numbers);
includes email, SMS, MMS, Instant Messaging and similar services;
voice Calls using standard telephone services are excluded.
Commercial Electronic Message:
an Electronic message which has a commercial purpose;
includes an offer to supply or sell goods or services or to advertise or promote goods;
includes for example and email sent offering to supply or promote educational services or business opportunities.
Unsolicited: Unasked for or sent without prior consent.
SPAM: Unsolicited commercial electronic messages.
Electronic account-holder: The individual or organisation that is responsible for the messaging account. This may be an email address or a telephone number.
